Termux:VA encoding for native Termux programs, on top of the pinned fork:
- per-picture key frames: an IDR or VP9 key frame the client asks for is sent
  to the daemon as ENC_UNIT_FORCE_KEY, and a changed target bitrate as
  ENC_UNIT_SET_BITRATE (daemon-patches/0001-livecd-encoder.patch);
- encoders are advertised only when the daemon lists a hardware component in
  "<socket>.encoders";
- where /dev/kgsl-3d0 is usable and nothing is configured, the bridge applies
  its KGSL settings itself, so a program that finds the GPU as a render node
  needs no TERMUX_VA_* variables;
- the visible picture is encoded: H.264 frame cropping and the HEVC
  conformance window crop the 16-aligned surfaces clients code, or 640x360
  comes out as 640x368;
- TERMUX_VA_DECODE=0 hides the decoders and leaves the encoders;
- per-call and per-surface traces are kept behind DMD_VA_LOG.

